Perfect. I’ve pushed the entire text-based PWA shell into the new public Prototypes repo: Sign In, one-shot intro handling, manifest and offline service worker are all there.
I also checked the actual V8 file. It’s 1.35 MB, and I hit the one awkward boundary I was hoping to avoid: although the GitHub connection can create binary blobs, I cannot feed it a local 1.35 MB binary file directly without stuffing roughly 1.8 MB of Base64 text through the connector. That is not a sensible or reliable way to handle the master asset.
So there is one manual upload, then I take over again:
	1.	Open arkaicolabs/Prototypes on GitHub.
	2.	Go into machine-precheck.
	3.	Create/open the folder assets.
	4.	Upload this exact file and name it intro-v8.mp4:
Download the frozen V8 master⁠￼
Once GitHub shows:
machine-precheck/assets/intro-v8.mp4
tell me “uploaded”.
Then I’ll verify the asset, finish GitHub Pages, check the deployment, and we’ll finally open the real thing on your iPhone. 📱